  "body": "### Summary\nAs a forum reader, I want each topic row to show the author of the last post (not the topic's starter) and the page count instead of the reply count, so that the row tells me who posted last and how long the topic is, with less noise.\n\n### Requested (operator, 2026-11-12)\n- The name of the topic's starter (first post) is useless in the topic lists. If a name is shown, it is the **author of the last post**.\n- The **page count** is enough: **remove the reply count** (\"N réponses\").\n\n### Today\n`App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/TopicRowView.swift:63-69` (`summary`): `⚑ cur / max` (flagged rows only) · `starterOrInterlocutors` · \"N réponses\" · relative date of the last post. The header comment (`:4-7`) records the starter and the replies as deliberate differences from legacy (GAP-026, 027).\n\n### Legacy (the reference this goes back to)\n`HFRswift/Swift/Favorites.swift` @ 87fe0d1c:\n- `:1100-1110`: page footer: `⚑ cur / max` on a flagged topic, otherwise `maxPage` alone (plus the poll mark).\n- `:1113-1120` (`trailingLabel`): `\"<author of last post> - <date of last post>\"` (`aAuthorOfLastPost`, `aDateOfLastPost`).\n\n### Scope\n- Topic lists using `TopicRowView` (`TopicListView`, `ForumSearchView`): show the page count on every row (the flagged `⚑ cur / max` footer stays; a row without a flag shows its page count, e.g. \"12 p.\" / \"12 pages\": wording to fix in the PR, legacy shows the bare number), then the **last post's author** (`TopicSummary.lastPost.author`, already parsed) and its relative date. Drop `starterOrInterlocutors` and the reply count from these rows.\n- MP lists: out of scope unless the operator says otherwise (there the interlocutor is the useful name).\n- VoiceOver: the combined label follows the same order.\n- Update the legacy pointer's `Differences:` and add a `gap-edit` of GAP-026 / GAP-027 in the PR's `### Ledger` (the row now matches legacy, apart from the relative date and the unread capsule).\n\n### Acceptance criteria\n- A favourites/topic list row shows: flag footer or page count · last post's author · relative date; no starter name, no reply count. Compact and regular density, Dynamic Type default and AX.\n- A row whose last post has no author parsed shows the rest without a dangling separator.\n- Tests on `summary` (or the rule it moves to): starter absent, last author present, no \"réponse(s)\", page count present on an unflagged row; shown to fail without the change.\n- Screenshots before/after on the PR (no real pseudos in committed fixtures or screenshots).\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_\n",
